Dear Ms Knight,

Would you please ask his Lordship not to read any of the information sent t=
o you by Mrs Zahmoul, in this message, or any other and pass the following t=
o his Lordship?

Thank you,

Alexis

=20

Dear Judge,

In respect of Mrs Zahmoul message below, I would ask you not to read the in=
formation she has submitted.

Mrs Zahmoul did not send a copy of her message to my instructing solicitors=
 in advance or when she sent the note to his Lordship.

I have not had a chance to look at the information. I am now engaged on oth=
er cases (as I am sure you are) and I cannot continue to give proper attenti=
on to these ad hoc to these further messages.

I understand Mrs Zahmoul continues to write directly to third parties about=
 the case. This must stop.=20

Would you please order Mrs Zahmoul to desist with contacting third parties =
about the case or sending evidence to the court pending your determination?

The evidence is closed. Mrs Zahmoul has solicitors on the record. If she wi=
shes to re-open the evidence (without our consent) she needs to make a forma=
l application to do so.=20

I apologise for the unsolicited message.

Best wishes,

Alexis Campbell

=20

